{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"TITLE:\"Analysis of gene expression in wild-type and Notch1 mutant retinal cells by single cell profiling.\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":50,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"23813500","source":"MED","pmid":"23813500","pmcid":"PMC3882027","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC3882027"]},"doi":"10.1002/dvdy.24006","title":"Analysis of gene expression in wild-type and Notch1 mutant retinal cells by single cell profiling.","authorString":"Mizeracka K, Trimarchi JM, Stadler MB, Cepko CL.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Mizeracka K","lastName":"Mizeracka","firstName":"Karolina","initials":"K","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Genetics, Department of Ophthalmology, Harvard Medical School, Boston, Massachusetts."}]}},{"fullName":"Trimarchi JM","lastName":"Trimarchi","firstName":"Jeffrey M","initials":"JM","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7923-1538"}},{"fullName":"Stadler MB","lastName":"Stadler","firstName":"Michael B","initials":"MB"},{"fullName":"Cepko CL","lastName":"Cepko","firstName":"Constance L","initials":"CL"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7923-1538"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"10","volume":"242","journalIssueId":2079046,"dateOfPublication":"2013 Oct","monthOfPublication":10,"yearOfPublication":2013,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Dev Dyn","title":"Developmental dynamics : an official publication of the American Association of Anatomists","essn":"1097-0177","issn":"1058-8388","isoabbreviation":"Dev Dyn","nlmid":"9201927"},"printPublicationDate":"2013-10-01"},"pubYear":"2013","pageInfo":"1147-1159","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>The vertebrate retina comprises sensory neurons, the photoreceptors, as well as many other types of neurons and one type of glial cell. These cells are generated by multipotent and restricted retinal progenitor cells (RPCs), which express Notch1. Loss of Notch1 in RPCs late during retinal development results in the overproduction of rod photoreceptors at the expense of interneurons and glia.<h4>Results</h4>To examine the molecular underpinnings of this observation, microarray analysis of single retinal cells from wild-type or Notch1 conditional knockout retinas was performed. In situ hybridization was carried out to validate some of the findings.<h4>Conclusions</h4>The majority of Notch1-mutant cells lost expression of known Notch target genes. These cells also had low levels of RPC and cell cycle genes, and robustly up-regulated rod precursor genes. In addition, single wild-type cells, in which cell cycle marker genes were down-regulated, expressed markers of both rod photoreceptors and interneurons.","affiliation":"Department of Genetics, Department of Ophthalmology, Harvard Medical School, Boston, Massachusetts.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Howard Hughes Medical Institute","acronym":"HHMI","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Institutes of Health","grantId":"R01EY09676","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NEI NIH HHS","acronym":"EY","grantId":"R01EY09676","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NEI NIH HHS","acronym":"EY","grantId":"R01 EY009676","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Stem Cells","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CY","qualifierName":"cytology"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Oligonucleotide Array Sequence Analysis"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Gene Expression Profiling"},{"majorTopic